  "kind": "case",
  "name": "The formula language: precedence, functions, values, and the errors that a formula can raise",
  "note": "Each case gives a formula and, optionally, the values of its variables. A case states either the value, or the error code. A formula with a literal zero divisor fails when it is read; the others fail when they are evaluated.",
  "cases": [
